Z||000016||stsmithgt||02-01-2001||01:09 PM||||On top of having to have a couple of sensors changed.  I had that, "it will idle as long as you don't try to go anywhere" syndrome.  It turned out to be my fuel pump.  My car would have to warm up first before that <I>idle only</I> rule would happen.  The fuel tank needs to be dropped to get it out so don't have a full tank. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/penny_spin_md_clr.gif"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/penny_spin_md_clr.gif"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Jake_Dragon||02-01-2001||05:03 PM||||Found a burnt wire going to the pump I don’t know if it is electrical fire or heat from the exhaust. Thanks for all your tips||||reg||1
Z||000018||Jake_Dragon||02-03-2001||05:45 PM||||Got it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> put in the new pump today, and the hose from the pump to the tube had a slit in it so I had pressure to a open container but as soon as I close the system the slit would open up and just cycle fuel in the tank. Now it runs but idles poorly so I looked under the car and the cat was glowing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Off to the parts store.||||reg||1
